                                                  \setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
                                                  \begin{document}$$Wx(s,\,\tau )\,=\,(1/s-1/2)\int x(t)\,\psi*\,((t-\tau )/s)\,{dt}$$\end{document}Wx(s,τ)=(1/s−1/2)∫x(t)ψ*((t−τ)/s)dtwhere s > 0 is the wavelet scale and τ is the time translation parameter. In discrete time, this integral is approximated through a convolution (via FFT) with appropriate zero-padding to mitigate edge effects (padding to next power-of-two length). The Morlet wavelet is typically written as2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
